## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical, implementable security controls for multi-tenant data on AWS, focusing on least-privilege access, data at rest encryption, and rapid breach containment.

## Key Concepts

- STS AssumeRole with tenant-scoped attributes
- S3 bucket policy and per-tenant prefixes for isolation
- KMS per-tenant CMKs with rotation
- CloudTrail data events for auditability
- 60-second containment workflow to revoke credentials and quarantine tenant data

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-bucket",
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-bucket/tenant-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:prefix": "tenant/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the 60-second containment workflow in a live environment?
- Which logging and alerting signals validate immutable audit trails during containment?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design automated, cross-account containment with tenant isolation, key lifecycle control, and immutable logs. Demonstrates threat modeling, policy boundaries, and incident runbook integration.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation across multiple AWS accounts
- Tenant-scoped KMS keys with rotation and key policy constraints
- Anomaly detection via CloudTrail Insights and GuardDuty
- Automated containment using EventBridge + Step Functions
- Immutable audit trails in CloudTrail and S3

## Code Example
```json
// Example KMS Key Policy (tenant-scoped)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Id": "tenant-key-policy",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_ID:role/tenant-access"},
      "Action": ["kms:Encrypt", "kms:Decrypt"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"aws:SourceAccount": "TENANT_ACCOUNT"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the containment workflow end-to-end before production?
- What metrics signal health of the containment and prevent false positives?

